   "html_text": "Marmura (1965, 183; 1981, 97) rejected the suggestion that al-Ghazālī might have held occasionalism and secondary causality as two cum-possible cosmological explanations. Marmura conceded that al-Ghazālī makes use of causalist language “sometimes in the way it is used in ordinary Arabic, sometimes in a more specifically Avicennian / Aristotelian way” and that this usage of language is innovative for the Ashʿarite school discourse (1995, 89). Yet in all major points of Muslim theology al-Ghazālī ",
